<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  Namer_AshfallSpire.xml                    UtinniPatches — new file 2026-09-12
  ============================================================================

  ASHFALL_SPIRE_LANDMARK_1. The Spire's display name must be the FIXED string
  "The Spire" (owner's register, ashfall_research_base.md §3/§6) — not one of
  the randomized outputs a vanilla landmark namer produces. The sw_Sarlacc
  placements are the counter-example this exists to avoid: the same LandmarkDef
  came back as "Hehieran Sarlacc", "Sarlacc Pit" and "The Sarlacc" on three
  different tiles, because NamerLandmark_* packs roll.

  🔑 THERE IS NO fixedName FIELD ON A LANDMARK. `LandmarkDef.nameMaker` is a
  RulePackDef and the only naming route the engine offers, so a fixed name has
  to be expressed as a rule pack that can only produce one string. Same shape
  as Namer_BlackstarCompany.xml in this folder: one rule, no alternatives, no
  weights — "a one-rule pack always produces the same string, so this is a
  fixed name in everything but mechanism."

  🔑 ROOT KEYWORD IS `r_name`, READ FROM THE ENGINE, not guessed:
  RimWorld/Planet/WorldLandmarks.cs:45 —
      landmark.name = NameGenerator.GenerateName(
          landmarkDef.nameMaker, null, appendNumberIfNameUsed: false, "r_name", null, null);
  so the single rule must be rooted at r_name or the landmark gets no name.

  ⛔ NO <include> ON PURPOSE. Every vanilla NamerLandmark_* pack pulls in
  WorldFeatureNamerCommon, which is what supplies [narrative_name],
  [NamePerson]'s ... and the terrain_word machinery that makes them vary.
  Including it here would hand the generator alternative r_name rules to roll
  against and reintroduce exactly the randomization this def exists to remove.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <RulePackDef>
    <defName>RUT_NamerLandmark_AshfallSpire</defName>
    <rulePack>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>r_name->The Spire</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </rulePack>
  </RulePackDef>

</Defs>
